The reacting **<HOMO> is the tertiary-amine <nitrogen> <lone pair>**. The relevant **<LUMO> is the C-I <antibonding orbital>, $\sigma^*_{\mathrm{C-I}}$, of MeI**. Backside lone-pair donation into that orbital forms N-C while weakening C-I. The neutral OH group is not first converted to an alkoxide in the stated reaction.

