\Image[paper-1-q2-amine-methylation.png]{title=Nitrogen lone-pair attack and iodide departure form choline iodide}

Draw a curly arrow from the <nitrogen> <lone pair> to methyl <carbon>, and a second from the C-I bond to I:
$$
\mathrm{HOCH_2CH_2NMe_2+MeI
\longrightarrow[HOCH_2CH_2NMe_3]^+I^-}.
$$
This is concerted **<SN2> quaternization**. The product is <choline> iodide; <nitrogen> has four <carbon> substituents and positive charge, while the <alcohol> remains OH.

= iii
{parent=b}
